The following maximum noise levels are allowed: Watercraft: Stationary Test - 88 dBA Lmax for boats manufactured before January 1, 1993; Microphone 3.3 feet from exhaust outlet - 5 feet above water.

The following maximum noise levels are allowed: Watercraft: Pass-By Test - 82 Lmax -measured 50ft from engine at 3,000rpm.', N'Watercraft noise levels were measured annually from 2009 to 2013 at 10 shorezone locations for five to six sampling periods (ranging from four to 12 days) from May through September. Sampling periods are comprised of both weekends and weekdays, allowing for analysis of the differences in noise levels or exceedances between days in the week. The monitoring periods include low, medium, and high watercraft use times throughout the day (7 AM to 7 PM). All noise events are individually analyzed and categorized by a trained noise technician.', 0, N'map', N'{"measures":[{"title":"Watercraft noise exceedances by site","sub":"Average daily exceedances of the shoreline watercraft noise standard in peak season (July to Labor Day). Choose a site.","layer":7,"x":"YEAR_OF_COUNT","y":"COUNT_VALUE","yName":"Exceedances per day","yLabel":"Exceedances per day","pick":"SITE_NAME","pickLabel":"Site","type":"bar","span":"span-12"}],"sitesLayer":{"layer":7,"name":"SITE_NAME","year":"YEAR_OF_COUNT"},"sitesPerYear":{"layer":7,"year":"YEAR_OF_COUNT","site":"SITE_NAME"}}', N'[{"Dashboard":"Threshold Dashboard","Label":"Post 1992 Watercraft-Stationary Test","Url":"https://thresholds.laketahoeinfo.org/threshold/indicators/43"},{"Dashboard":"Threshold Dashboard","Label":"Pre-1993 Watercraft-Stationary Test","Url":"https://thresholds.laketahoeinfo.org/threshold/indicators/42"},{"Dashboard":"Threshold Dashboard","Label":"Watercraft Pass-By Test","Url":"https://thresholds.laketahoeinfo.org/threshold/indicators/40"}]');

The maximum 24-hour CNEL A-weighted decibel (dBA) is used to assess status. The annual mean CNEL is used to assess trend. The A-weighted decibel measurement is used in evaluating the effects of environmental and industrial noise effects on human health.', N'Historical monitoring consisted of gathering a single 24-hour sample in various land use areas. Threshold standard attainment status was based on a single sample representing each land use type. In contrast to single-sample historic monitoring, a more comprehensive CNEL monitoring protocol was implemented in 2011. The 2011 monitoring approach was based on recommendations provided by a noise expert (Brown-Buntin Associates 2004). The approach since 2011 monitors the same sites every year for at least seven days during the period of May 15 to October 1. This captures noise levels during the construction season and the busiest tourist seasons. Unusual noise such as lightning strikes and animal sounds are discarded from the data. The mean 24-hour dBA from each day is averaged for the final CNEL at each monitoring location. Decibel levels at night are weighted heavier to account for human’s greater sensitivity to night-time noise.', 0, N'map', N'{"measures":[{"title":"Noise in critical wildlife habitat","sub":"Average CNEL of all critical wildlife habitat sites, by monitoring period, in decibels.","layer":74,"where":"Category = ''Critical Wildlife Habitat''","x":"Year","xType":"category","xLabel":"Period","y":"Value","yName":"Average CNEL","yLabel":"Average CNEL (dB)","type":"bar","standard":{"field":"Threshold_Value"},"span":"span-6"},{"title":"Critical wildlife habitat noise by site","sub":"Maximum-day CNEL at each critical wildlife habitat site, in decibels.","layer":6,"where":"CNEL_LAND_USE = ''CRITICAL WILDLIFE HABITAT''","x":"YEAR_OF_COUNT","y":"COUNT_VALUE","yLabel":"CNEL (dB)","seriesBy":"SITE_NAME","seriesLabel":"Site","type":"bar","standard":{"value":45},"span":"span-6"},{"title":"Noise in transportation corridors","sub":"Average CNEL at each highway monitoring site, in decibels, against the corridor limit. Choose a highway.","layer":11,"x":"YEAR_OF_COUNT","y":"CNEL_AVG_VALUE","yLabel":"Average CNEL (dB)","seriesBy":"SITE_NAME","seriesLabel":"Site","pick":"HIGHWAY","pickLabel":"Highway","pickDefault":"50","standard":{"field":"CNEL_LIMIT","label":"Corridor limit"},"type":"bar","span":"span-12"}],"sitesLayer":{"layer":6,"name":"SITE_NAME","year":"YEAR_OF_COUNT","where":"CNEL_LAND_USE = ''CRITICAL WILDLIFE HABITAT''"},"sitesPerYear":{"layer":6,"year":"YEAR_OF_COUNT","site":"SITE_NAME","where":"CNEL_LAND_USE = ''CRITICAL WILDLIFE HABITAT''"}}', N'[{"Dashboard":"Threshold Dashboard","Label":"Critical Wildlife Habitat Areas","Url":"https://thresholds.laketahoeinfo.org/threshold/indicators/29"}]');

The following maximum noise levels are allowed: Aircraft measured 6,500 m-start of takeoff roll 2,000 m-runway threshold approach: N1: The following maximum noise levels are allowed: Aircraft measured 6,500 m-start of takeoff roll 2,000 m-runway threshold approach.', N'Lake Tahoe Airport monitored noise at six sites in the vicinity of the airport (see

map above) following an approved monitoring protocol. All exceedances logged by these monitors are documented and categorized in quarterly and annual noise reports sent to TRPA. While monitoring of

exceedances has continued, the ability to differentiate between aircraft and non-aircraft exceedances was not possible, therefore data quality is low and only total exceedances (including aircraft, natural sources (e.g. wind, lightning, wildlife) and other anthropogenic sources) are reported and trend is not assessed.

Past monitoring data shows that an average of 17 percent of exceedances were caused by aircraft, however the percent of exceedances per year caused by aircraft varies greatly year to year, making any judgement on how many of the total exceedances are caused by aircraft in any given year inestimable.', 0, N'charts', N'{"measures":[{"title":"Airport single noise event exceedances","sub":"Single noise events above the standard at Lake Tahoe Airport each year. Approximate: read from the published chart image.","json":"data/threshold-evaluation/aircraft-noise-exceedances.json","sourceHref":"https://thresholds.laketahoeinfo.org/ThresholdIndicator/Detail/100","sourceLabel":"Threshold Dashboard chart (image)","x":"Year","y":"Exceedances","yName":"Exceedances","yLabel":"Exceedances","type":"bar","span":"span-12"}]}', N'[{"Dashboard":"Threshold Dashboard","Label":"Aircraft Noise Departure/Arrival (8 AM To 8 PM)","Url":"https://thresholds.laketahoeinfo.org/threshold/indicators/38"},{"Dashboard":"Threshold Dashboard","Label":"Aircraft Noise Departure/Arrival (8 PM To 8 AM)","Url":"https://thresholds.laketahoeinfo.org/threshold/indicators/39"}]');

